adjudication.rationale:
In `CredentialHelper.createRecoveryCodesCredential(...)`, JSON serialization is done in a try/catch and any `IOException` is rethrown as `new RuntimeException(e)` with no message/context (no realm/user info):
```java
try { recoveryCodesJson = JsonSerialization.writeValueAsString(generatedCodes); }
catch (IOException e) { throw new RuntimeException(e); }
```
This matches the finding: if serialization fails, the operator gets an unattributed RuntimeException on the required-action path, unlike the success path which logs the username. It’s an observability/diagnostics concern rather than a verifiable functional defect from the diff alone.
